From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:42:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sleep: Say what apple-s2r gives USB across a
 sleep

Aurora's ATC/USB sleep work has the Type-C PHY, the dwc3 glue and the
port controllers ask the sleep driver about the USB-C debug link and
about a USB host that sleeps in place. Its T8140 driver answers from
what its commit sequence does: it cuts the debug link with a cold reset
of one port controller, and it lowers ATC0_USB_AON unless the host
sleeps in place.

apple-s2r does neither. It lowers no ATC power domain itself (runtime PM
and genpd own them until the SoC goes down as a whole) and cuts no debug
link, and no PHY it serves can take a host through hibernation: that
needs the controller power control only the T8140 PHY maps. So give
these entries as stubs, as apple_sleep_debug_link_cut() already is: no
debug link was cut, there is nothing to keep for a host asleep, and no
port has a USB wake to arm. The drivers then stop the controller for a
deep sleep and start it again after, and their T8140 paths stay unused.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 include/linux/soc/apple/sleep.h | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/soc/apple/sleep.h b/include/linux/soc/apple/sleep.h
index f1ce68ee12..7d14b5e95a 100644
--- a/include/linux/soc/apple/sleep.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/apple/sleep.h
@@ -121,4 +121,37 @@ static inline bool apple_sleep_debug_link_cut(void)
 	return false;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Nor does a sleep here cold-reset a port controller to end one: there is no
+ * debug link to rearm and no setup to expect from that after the wake.
+ */
+static inline bool apple_sleep_debug_link_was_cut(struct device *dev)
+{
+	return false;
+}
+
+static inline bool apple_sleep_debug_link_cut_peek(struct device *dev)
+{
+	return false;
+}
+
+/*
+ * A USB host that sleeps in place (see apple_atcphy_sleep_prepare()) needs its
+ * PHY's controller power control, which only Aurora's T8140 PHY has. apple-s2r
+ * lowers no ATC power domain itself, so there is no USB_AON domain to keep for
+ * such a host, and as none sleeps in place, no port has a USB wake to arm.
+ */
+static inline void apple_sleep_usb_set_asleep(bool asleep)
+{
+}
+
+static inline void apple_sleep_usb_set_wake_ports(unsigned long ports)
+{
+}
+
+static inline bool apple_sleep_usb_port_can_wake(unsigned int port)
+{
+	return false;
+}
+
 #endif /* _LINUX_SOC_APPLE_SLEEP_H_ */
